1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,447
What if you could never die?

2
00:00:01,727 --> 00:00:02,905
Not a longer life.

3
00:00:03,185 --> 00:00:04,312
No end at all.

4
00:00:04,662 --> 00:00:05,376
At first,

5
00:00:05,476 --> 00:00:06,753
it feels like a gift.

6
00:00:07,033 --> 00:00:08,001
Every language.

7
00:00:08,281 --> 00:00:09,166
Every place.

8
00:00:09,446 --> 00:00:10,470
No deadlines.

9
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:12,296
No fear of running out of

10
00:00:12,296 --> 00:00:12,593
time.

11
00:00:12,943 --> 00:00:13,552
Today,

12
00:00:13,652 --> 00:00:16,535
the average person lives about seventy-three

13
00:00:16,535 --> 00:00:16,928
years.

14
00:00:17,208 --> 00:00:19,132
The longest verified life ever?

15
00:00:19,412 --> 00:00:20,811
One hundred twenty-two.

16
00:00:21,161 --> 00:00:22,806
You would blow past that record,

17
00:00:22,906 --> 00:00:23,904
and keep going.

18
00:00:24,184 --> 00:00:26,334
A thousand years is eight times

19
00:00:26,334 --> 00:00:28,094
the longest life on record.

20
00:00:28,794 --> 00:00:30,675
But everyone you love would grow

21
00:00:30,675 --> 00:00:30,903
old,

22
00:00:31,003 --> 00:00:31,778
and leave.

23
00:00:32,058 --> 00:00:32,674
Again,

24
00:00:32,774 --> 00:00:33,544
and again,

25
00:00:33,644 --> 00:00:34,397
and again.

26
00:00:34,677 --> 00:00:36,426
Even their faces would fade.

27
00:00:36,776 --> 00:00:38,337
Cities would rise and fall.

28
00:00:38,617 --> 00:00:40,389
Whole languages would vanish.

29
00:00:40,669 --> 00:00:42,471
Every country you knew would become

30
00:00:42,471 --> 00:00:43,071
a footnote.

31
00:00:43,421 --> 00:00:45,161
In about half a billion years,

32
00:00:45,261 --> 00:00:47,227
Earth may no longer support most

33
00:00:47,227 --> 00:00:47,644
plants.

34
00:00:47,924 --> 00:00:48,979
In about a billion,

35
00:00:49,079 --> 00:00:50,750
its oceans could boil away.

36
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:51,614
Then,

37
00:00:51,714 --> 00:00:53,872
roughly five billion years from now,

38
00:00:53,972 --> 00:00:55,699
the Sun swells into a red

39
00:00:55,699 --> 00:00:56,082
giant.

40
00:00:56,362 --> 00:00:58,434
Earth is not expected to survive.

41
00:00:59,134 --> 00:00:59,957
But you would.

42
00:01:00,237 --> 00:01:01,570
Drifting through space,

43
00:01:01,670 --> 00:01:02,342
alive,

44
00:01:02,442 --> 00:01:03,269
in the dark,

45
00:01:03,369 --> 00:01:04,755
with nothing left to see.

46
00:01:05,455 --> 00:01:06,666
Nothing could end you.

47
00:01:06,946 --> 00:01:08,304
Nothing could change you.

48
00:01:08,584 --> 00:01:10,217
Maybe what gives life meaning,

49
00:01:10,317 --> 00:01:11,430
is that it ends.

50
00:01:11,710 --> 00:01:12,870
Every moment counts,

51
00:01:12,970 --> 00:01:14,061
because it's limited.

52
00:01:14,761 --> 00:01:15,297
So,

53
00:01:15,397 --> 00:01:16,369
would you take it?

